{
  "comment": [
    "Built-in I/O boundary catalog. Each entry marks calls to a known transmit/receive API.",
    "match: exactly one of 'name' (exact) or 'prefix' (covers _IT/_DMA style variants).",
    "direction is the API's documented contract: in = data arrives, out = data leaves, inout = both.",
    "requiresTypeRef / requiresDependency: any one listed fact must co-occur in the calling file.",
    "Member-call languages (C#, Python, C++ field calls) store only the member name, so their",
    "entries MUST be gated - an ungated 'Write' would flood every workspace with false stubs.",
    "Generic bare C names (read, write, printf) are deliberately absent for the same reason."
  ],
